- BIRTHDATE: Older clients might have more stable credit history; very young clients might have less credit history.
- SEX: Gender usually has no causal effect on credit score.
- EDU (education level): Higher education often correlates with better income and creditworthiness.
- INCOME: Higher income usually positively correlates with credit score.
- TERM: Longer credit terms might imply higher trust or better credit score.
- Credit history rating: Better ratings (A1, A2, A3, B1, B2, B3) indicate better credit scoring; worse ratings (C1, C2, C3, D1, D2, D3, E1, E2, E3) indicate worse credit.
